{
  "_comment": [
    "Goals conceded WHILE ON THE PITCH, as a table of cases both languages read.",
    "",
    "app.js and daily_pull.py each implement this, because each is a writer and a",
    "stat that two writers disagree about is exactly the bug this replaces. Two",
    "implementations need one specification, so it lives here rather than being",
    "written out twice and drifting the first time somebody fixes only one.",
    "",
    "THE WINDOW RULE, which every case below is an instance of: a goal counts",
    "against a player when start < minute <= end. A starter has start 0, so every",
    "goal from the first minute counts. A substitute has start = the minute he came",
    "on, and the man he replaced has end = that same minute -- so a goal in the",
    "minute of a substitution belongs to exactly one of them, never both and never",
    "neither. The two windows tile.",
    "",
    "END = 100000 stands for 'was still on at the final whistle'. A literal 90",
    "would drop stoppage-time goals, which is the half of the match this rule is",
    "most often asked about.",
    "",
    "ORIENTATION. A substitution event names two players and this repo cannot verify which of API-Football's `player` and `assist` holds the one coming ON. So nothing here depends on it: a case may set \"swap\": true to build the same substitution with the two fields exchanged, and it must produce byte-identical windows. Reading it the wrong way round was silent and cost a real manager points -- a midfielder on for the last five minutes, after both goals, charged for both.",
    "",
    "OWN GOALS have the same problem and the same answer. The feed may file one under the side whose player put it in, or under the side credited with the goal, and nothing here may depend on which: a case may set \"og_swap\": true to file it under the other side, and must produce identical results. The orientation is resolved from the SCORELINE, which each side's conceded count has to equal. Reported from the app as a goalkeeper who won 4-0, was charged one goal conceded, and lost the clean sheet he had plainly kept."
  ],
  "end_sentinel": 100000,
